{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_rwrxmfn43zct4euegdrfk2knib6owtqusv7bp4qswohlns3p74pq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 37 tests pass. Summary:\n\n**Phase 1 (Translation):** I translated the C SAT collision-detection library to safe, idiomatic Rust:\n- Replaced every `unimplemented!()` body in `src/satc.rs`.\n- Avoided `unsafe`, FFI, and external crates — pure safe Rust.\n- The C library uses pointer-based mutating operations on `double *` points; in Rust I converted these to value-returning functions that take `&[f64; 2]` and return `[f64; 2]`.\n- Carefully matched C semantics including its known quirk in `satc_point_rotate` (`y = x*sin - y*cos`).\n- Added a private `polygon_recalc` helper to compute calc_points/edges/normals when a polygon is created or its points are replaced.\n\n**Phase 2 (Tests):** I created `src/bin/test_satc.rs` with 37 `#[test]` functions covering every module / public function. All expected values were obtained by writing and running a C ground-truth program that links against the original `c_src/satc.h`. Tests cover:\n- All point math primitives (perp, reverse, add, sub, scale_xy, scale_x, rotate, normalize incl. zero-vector edge case, project, reflect, copy, create).\n- Voronoi regions (left, middle, right).\n- `flatten_points_on`, `is_separating_axis` (both separating and overlapping cases).\n- Circle/polygon/box construction, including verification of computed `calc_points`, `edges`, and `normals`.\n- AABB computation for both circles and polygons.\n- Centroid (square and triangle).\n- Point-in-circle and point-in-polygon (including the small hexagon test).\n- All four collision tests: circle-circle (collide / no-collide), polygon-polygon (collide / no-collide), polygon-circle, and circle-polygon.\n- All public constants.\n\n`cargo test`: **37 passed; 0 failed**."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_